+### Images that are still only on CarrierWave keep being displayed
+
+Some images that can be seen today are still only where CarrierWave stored them, and this deploy can't break
+them, whether the copy is over or not:
+
+- images that haven't been copied yet (copy not run or not finished, `failed`, `changed`);
+- `unsupported` images (eg. SVG), which Active Storage wouldn't serve as images;
+- CarrierWave images newer than their Active Storage copy (stored by the release before step 1, after a
+  rollback).
